* QueueDesk lab topology. Re-runnable: REPLACE keeps definitions converging.
DEFINE QLOCAL('QUEUEDESK.INSTRUCTION.IN') DEFPSIST(YES) MAXDEPTH(5000) REPLACE
* Operational hold for poison. Routing is APPLICATION-owned (QUAR-01): the worker
* counts JMSXDeliveryCount and moves the message itself after three failed
* processing deliveries. BOTHRESH(0) disables the JMS client's own poison logic
* on purpose: when the client intercepts a broken route it throws JMSWMQ1080
* inside the listener container's receive call, where no application hook can
* turn it into a clean stop. Proved by probe 2026-10-05; see RUNBOOK-L3.
* BOQNAME below is documentation only at threshold 0. The app never consumes
* from BACKOUT; the reconciler only browses it.
DEFINE QLOCAL('QUEUEDESK.INSTRUCTION.BACKOUT') DEFPSIST(YES) MAXDEPTH(5000) REPLACE
ALTER QLOCAL('QUEUEDESK.INSTRUCTION.IN') BOQNAME('QUEUEDESK.INSTRUCTION.BACKOUT') BOTHRESH(0)
* B04 risk harness isolation (RS01-RS06): the risk-eval app boots against its
* own database and these queues, so harness traffic never races the live
* backend or other lanes. Same application-owned routing contract as above;
* the existing QUEUEDESK.** auth profile already covers the app principal.
DEFINE QLOCAL('QUEUEDESK.RISK.EVAL.IN') DEFPSIST(YES) MAXDEPTH(5000) REPLACE
DEFINE QLOCAL('QUEUEDESK.RISK.EVAL.BACKOUT') DEFPSIST(YES) MAXDEPTH(5000) REPLACE
ALTER QLOCAL('QUEUEDESK.RISK.EVAL.IN') BOQNAME('QUEUEDESK.RISK.EVAL.BACKOUT') BOTHRESH(0)
